# <%= mockProjectName %>

Mock API server for <%= projectName %> using JSON Server.

## Configuration

The mock server can be configured using environment variables. Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and modify as needed:

```bash
cp .env.example .env
```

### Environment Variables

| Variable | Description | Default |
|----------|-------------|---------|
| `HOST` | Server hostname | `localhost` |
| `PORT` | Server port number | `3001` |
| `DEBUG` | Enable debug logging | `false` |
| `CORS_ORIGIN` | CORS allowed origin | `*` |
| `DB_PATH` | Path to database file | `./data/db.json` |

### Example .env file

```env
HOST=localhost
PORT=8080
DEBUG=true
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:4200
DB_PATH=./data/custom-db.json
```

## Overview

This mock server provides a RESTful API for development and testing purposes. It simulates a real backend with realistic data and supports all standard HTTP methods.

## Available Endpoints

All API responses follow a standardized format:

